## Step 1 — CLI help, `?` with NO CR (qmark.py; Ctrl-U self-test passed) (evidence/5082/5082-q-if-u5.out, -q-if2-u5.out)
```
(config-if)#ipv6 address ?          WORD (Prefix name delegated from parent PD server) | X:X::X:X/M | autoconfig | dhcp | suffix
(config-if)#ipv6 dhcp client pd ?   WORD  Prefix name delegated from parent PD server
(config-if)#ipv6 address ck5082pd ::/96 ?        eui64 | <cr>
(config-if)#ipv6 address 2001:db8:5082::/96 ?    anycast | eui64 | <cr>
(config-if)#ipv6 nd prefix ?        WORD (Prefix name delegated from parent PD server) | X:X::X:X/M | auto-advertise
(config-if)#ipv6 nd prefix 2001:db8:5082::/128 ? <0-4294967295> Valid lifetime (secs) | <cr>
(config-if)#ipv6 nd prefix ck5082pd 2001:db8:5082::/65 ?  <5-315360000> | infinite | <cr>
```
The parser offers `<cr>` at every prefix length, so any refusal must come when the command executes.

