## Step 4 — the same length check on a LITERAL eui64 address: enforced (13:25:24–13:25:52, evidence/5082/5082-s3cfg-u5.out, -s3cfg2-u5.out)
```
IE520-stk(config-if)#ipv6 address 2001:db8:5083::/96 eui64
% Prefix length must not be more than 64
IE520-stk(config-if)#ipv6 address 2001:db8:5083::/65 eui64
% Prefix length must not be more than 64
IE520-stk(config-if)#ipv6 address 2001:db8:5083::/128 eui64
% Bad mask /128 for address 2001:db8:5083::
IE520-stk(config-if)#ipv6 address 2001:db8:5084::/64 eui64          (accepted — control)
IE520-stk(config-if)#no ipv6 nd suppress-ra                          (accepted)
```
⇒ The platform has the eui64 length check, but only on the literal-prefix path. The PD path (step 2)
bypasses it.

