⇒ The illegal /65, /96, /127 and /128 prefixes are on the wire with the autonomous flag set.

## Observation O-1 — prefix delegation not established on this bench (not graded)
The aim was to exercise the accepted PD + eui64 lines with a real delegated prefix. The AR4050S (u1)
was made a PD server on vlan10: `ipv6 local pool ck5082 2001:db8:5000::/48 56`, `ipv6 dhcp pool ck5082` /
`prefix-delegation pool ck5082`, `interface vlan10` `ipv6 enable` + `ipv6 dhcp server ck5082`. The stack's
PD client was moved to its vlan10 (`ipv6 enable`, `ipv6 dhcp client pd ck5082pd`). After ~60 s
(evidence/5082/5082-pd-*.out):
```
4050  show counter ipv6 dhcp-server : SOLICIT in 6, ADVERTISE out 6, REQUEST in 0, REPLY out 0
stack show counter ipv6 dhcp-client : SOLICIT out 754 (lifetime, all interfaces), ADVERTISE in 0, REQUEST out 0
stack show ipv6 dhcp interface vlan10 : Prefix name ck5082pd / prefix is not received
4050  ping ipv6 fe80::200:cdff:fe37:d6f%vlan10 repeat 3 : 3/3; ND entry for the stack on sa1, and the stack's for the 4050
```
The server answers, link-local unicast works both ways, and the DUT's DHCPv6 client never counts an
ADVERTISE. The cause was not investigated (sentinel scope ruling). So the delegation was not
established on this bench, and the accepted PD + eui64 config could not be exercised. It may bear on
T5093 (DHCPv6 relay, queue row 10). The 4050 PD config was removed in teardown.

